WEBVTT

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.260
Is this... a dream?

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.170
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.870
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>Let's share a selfish kiss!</i>

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:04.500
<i>The petals of this flower fall in the wind</i>

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:10.170
<i>The stars are more than I could count</i>

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>I could place all the blame on you,</i>

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>swallowing back my tears,</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.930
<i>but I can't tell anyone about how my heart races</i>

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.320
<i>(Reach out)</i>

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.610
<i>Until it all breaks apart</i>

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.560
<i>(Reach out)</i>

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.790
<i>Until you can take flight</i>

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.280
<i>(To the ends)</i>

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.160
<i>Deep in my heart</i>

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>(Of time)</i>

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.480
<i>There is a prayer</i>

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:35.650
<i>Just feel, just believe</i>

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:39.720
<i>and speed through it all</i>

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.910
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.720
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:51.340
<i>Let's share a kiss faster than light, just wait for me</i>

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.960
<i>I'll leave my body behind</i>

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.880
<i>I'll leave my heart beating hard</i>

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.280
<i>I'll break free from these chains holding me down</i>

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:08.990
<i>Just come get me, in my purest form</i>

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.570
First Lt. Mirage and Second Lt. Hayate, please take care of the solar panel repairs at L36.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.030
Roger.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:25.510
First Lt. Chuck, please head to outer area B3 and clear the debris.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.450
First Lt. Chuck?

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:28.960
Right...

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.340
He still doesn't know if his family is safe.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.170
Yeah...

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:41.590
As you can see, the island ship's fold reactors could fail at any moment.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:45.810
However, we don't have the 
necessary resources to repair them.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.490
We're going to run out of power and air eventually.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:50.560
What are our options?

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.190
Having it dock to the Elysion is the only thing that makes sense.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.110
The Macross-class reactors should be able to handle the combined load,

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:02.590
but the island ship's docking system was also damaged.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:09.830
<i>Food will be next distributed in the refugee area at 1600.</i>

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:16.000
<i>I repeat. Food will be next distributed in the refugee area at 1600.</i>

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.290
I never thought Ragna would get caught up in the war.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:16.000
I wanna go home!

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.510
My daughter is missing!

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:19.760
She was with me when we boarded!

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.420
We had an old lady, and...

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:22.890
Please calm down.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:25.190
We have a designated location where people can check in.

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:26.460
I'd suggest trying that—

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:28.890
What's going on?

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:29.900
I'm scared!

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:30.940
Is everything okay?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.960
There's no need to worry!

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.920
They're working their hardest to repair everything so I'm sure we'll be fine!

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.360
Is that true?

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.670
You betcha!

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:41.890
Lying makes your teeth rot!

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:42.950
Freyja!

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.080
You guys...

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.220
Everything's all right now.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.790
Sorry I wasn't there.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.500
Bro...

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:57.460
Where's Marianne, though?

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.380
She closed the door in front of us and...

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:07.510
She'll be fine.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.230
We're talking about Marianne. She'll be fine.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.170
What's going on?

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.310
Resting is a part of your duty too.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.820
Can't we do something to help the civilians left on Ragna?

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:28.490
The ruins further amplified the enemy's singing.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:32.340
We can't enter the globular cluster.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:34.730
We should at least do some recon!

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:37.500
We can't afford to split up our forces.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.070
Ragna is my home.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:43.050
My family and friends are still there!

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.140
We share the same sentiments.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:49.930
Calm down.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.630
My apologies.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:54.020
Are the people on Ragna safe?

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:01.110
This is footage from one of our 
agents who remained on Ragna.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:05.570
Just like it was in Voldor, they are not harming civilians.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.740
They even supply them with food and water.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:10.880
Apples and water?!

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:13.400
They're doing it so they can control them with the Var!

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:15.800
Sorry.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:16.370
Don't worry.

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.720
Are we really just going to sit here and watch?

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:24.170
At this point in time, we don't 
have enough ammo or fuel.

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:26.260
We don't even have the funds to buy more.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.130
Chaos is a civilian contractor.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:31.970
We need contracts and money to function.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:36.020
Didn't we have a defense commission from the globular cluster alliance?

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.830
That very alliance is basically destroyed now.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:44.030
Even though our contract is intact, we can't expect payments anytime soon.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:50.040
For now, the most we can do is to 
protect the civilians on board this ship.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.920
A whirl of sad and frightened voices.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.460
A fake sky.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:04.310
The sky I saw in my dream was so radiant.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:11.140
We have successfully withdrawn all of our forces.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:16.490
I'm told the song of Windermere can be heard across the cluster.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:22.420
All ruins have activated and are actively generating a special fold sound field

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:25.530
that has the capability to interfere with the mental functions of sentient life forms.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:30.260
This field, which envelops the cluster, 
accelerates the Var symptoms of those within

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.870
and allows for mind control.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:38.600
However, the song's effects are 
much milder than anticipated.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:42.630
We suspect that they haven't completely 
figured out the abilities of the ruins either.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:46.090
What about fold jamming?

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:52.320
This was the first time we deployed it against the Wind Singer, so the results were not clear.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.940
If only the operation had succeeded 7 years ago, it wouldn't have come to this.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.020
Bringing that up won't get us anywhere.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.890
Take care of it quickly.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:01.550
Yes, sir.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:10.360
When is the funeral?

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:13.840
As soon as we return to Windermere.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:16.830
But before that, we shall 
have the coronation ceremony.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:20.890
You shall become our king.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.170
Even our White Knight...

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:30.580
Just how many lives will they take from us?

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.200
When can we get home?

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:37.390
This place is so boring.

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:40.010
One for you. And one for you.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:43.830
Are you okay?

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:46.570
You should drink something.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.650
Thanks.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:52.330
Freyja, you should take a break.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.860
Oh, 'kay.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.330
I...

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:57.500
What?

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.130
Uh...

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:04.310
I forgot to feed Querule! I'll be right back!

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:09.090
But Querule's right here...

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:13.410
Let's check on block 9 once we're done eating.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.580
Okay.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.350
Is this gonna be all right?

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:19.220
This thing hasn't been in space for the last 30 years.

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:23.730
The damage it took during the escape from Ragna isn't completely repaired yet either.

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:26.020
Who knows what's going to happen?

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.610
What about Chuck?

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.570
Dunno. I figure he wants to be left alone now.

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:36.740
I see. I'm worried about him.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.450
You snooze, you lose!

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.950
How could you just steal someone's food like that?!

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:46.380
Chill, it's just an apple slice.

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:50.990
But we're almost out of canned sea apples...

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:52.010
Ah!

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.790
I almost forgot.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:59.340
Mirage! Thanks a bundle for saving me the other day!

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:02.520
I never got the chance to say it.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:06.460
Don't worry about it. Protecting Walküre is my job.

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:13.200
Those things can live out of water?

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:17.030
Let's hope we can return to Ragna soon.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.160
Yeah! I wanna go back!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.730
It's where I got to meet you all and where all my dreams came true.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:26.560
Of course I love Windermere too,

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.460
but at this point I love Ragna just as much.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.460
Home, huh?

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:38.120
My late dad was a soldier and 
my mom was an army medic,

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.750
so we never stayed long in one place.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:43.910
The concept of "home" is just not ingrained in me.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:46.480
Is that so?

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:48.880
What did your father do in the army?

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.190
I don't know the details.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.560
He was pretty eccentric.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.780
He kept sending me weird stuff from places he'd gone to.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:01.850
Like seashells and sand and he once 
even sent me a snowman in a cooler.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:05.080
He'd always attach a handwritten note.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.750
Never outright said where exactly he was,

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:15.060
just stuff like "the sea is blue," "the desert's scorching," or "the snow numbs the skin."

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:16.840
Short descriptions like that.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:19.930
This is also one of his gifts.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:22.580
That's a fold quartz, right?

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.890
Yeah. No idea how he got it.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:28.200
Your dad sounds like a great person.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.600
You think so?

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.150
But with a childhood like that,

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:36.510
I couldn't find anything I really 
wanted to do after leaving home.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:42.230
I traveled to a bunch of places, 
but nothing felt quite right.

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:47.530
Then I came to Ragna, got in a VF-31, and the wind just felt so nice.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:53.210
I thought I could maybe figure something out here.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:59.800
Me too. I think Ragna's changed me a little.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:01.820
You too?

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:02.640
Tell me more!

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:06.420
I could finally feel at ease.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:10.750
I felt I could find something new... Just like that.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:14.590
So not just anywhere but somewhere I want to go?

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:15.360
Huh?

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:18.590
Anyway, the sky is too low here.

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:21.610
We can't stay here forever.

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:22.570
Yup!

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:23.320
Yeah.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:27.840
Again?

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:30.230
The power supply is still unstable.

00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:33.540
What's going on?

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:36.690
It's still not coming back up?

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:38.210
Makina, status?

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.170
Not looking good.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:45.120
The island ship's main reactor is down to 28% output.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:48.870
Cooler units 1 through 3 of the Nerith block are down.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.640
Ditto for units 8 to 10.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:54.350
That stuff happens when you take off without warming up first.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.570
Excess energy in block E-17?!

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.530
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.140
A-Are we okay?

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.560
Go up to the surface, Freyja.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.290
We'll go investigate the blocks ahead.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:13.820
Roger.

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:15.830
Wind?

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:21.720
Gravity control system malfunction in area E, block 17!

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:25.640
We've detected a hull breach. Air is escaping!

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.990
Was it cause of that explosion earlier?

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:32.310
Wh-What's going on?!

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:34.350
Freyja!

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:34.940
Hayate!

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:37.980
Freyja!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.440
Hayate!

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:47.070
Seal it off quickly!

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.870
Check how much air we have left!

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.490
Prioritize supplying power to the life support systems!

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:01.460
Block E-17 has been sealed off.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:03.780
Are you okay, Freyja?

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:07.840
Well, at least I didn't get ejected from the ship.

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:10.470
You always were a lucky girl.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:16.920
I'll be you guys' catastrophe respaws team!

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:25.910
Main reactor's output down to 21%.

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:28.530
The temperature in the island ship is down to 16°C.

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:30.990
Captain!

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.860
I know this is getting ahead of the plan...

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:35.580
...but we should get on with the thing now.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.790
Are you ready?

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:41.200
Rei-Rei's already fixed the software.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:44.500
Once the current repairs are complete, we're good to go.

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:46.010
Trouble in the rubble, Makina!

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:50.680
To get this moving, we'd need 
to connect the cables in E-17.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:52.430
That's...

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.260
...where the explosion was earlier.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.140
We'll go.

00:13:58.410 --> 00:13:59.800
Haya-Haya?

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:02.440
We're near E-17.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.320
Connecting a cable should be easy enough!

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:05.470
Counting on you!

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:07.950
Thanks, Haya-Haya!

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.490
Let's get going.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.120
We've got...

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:15.500
...work to do too.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:23.380
<i>Hayate and Mirage are still in there.</i>

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.780
We're running out of air too.

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:35.720
We should've just stayed on Ragna.

00:14:56.600 --> 00:15:00.580
<i>We never know what the future will bring</i>

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:04.800
<i>We just believe that there's a silver lining</i>

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:03.000
So pretty...

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.800
Walküre...

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:09.050
<i>There's no need to fear and one thing to do</i>

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:13.050
<i>Overcome all difficulties we face</i>

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:16.810
<i>Sadness is a trap</i>

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:21.440
<i>Morning wanders in with secrets</i>

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.320
<i>The flowers are wet with tears</i>

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:30.030
<i>Ordeals aren't restricted by logic</i>

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:38.540
<i>We just follow our instincts and do our best</i>

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.540
Yay!

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:42.580
<i>Wherever you are, just remember</i>

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.580
Can we really fix this?

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:44.710
We'll manage!

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:47.170
<i>to look up at the stars</i>

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.170
Manage, he says...

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:51.180
<i>When you're searching for answers</i>

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:55.470
<i>Your sighs are beautiful and faint</i>

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:52.380
Hurry up!

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.060
I'm coming!

00:15:55.470 --> 00:16:03.230
<i>This blue planet has an everlasting wish</i>

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:08.480
<i>We have to pass it down</i>

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:10.500
Have you connected the pipelines yet?

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:12.740
Just a little more! Hold on!

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:19.870
I'm not gonna let it end here!

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.730
<i>The backup power line connects here.</i>

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:26.750
You know how this works?

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:29.900
I've done my share of odd jobs in the past.

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:33.010
So when the platoon fires you, you'll be fine!

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:36.540
You make it sound like that's gonna happen for sure.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.260
This should do it.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.750
Anything I can help with?

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:43.520
We just need to open the 
emergency valve on the other side.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.580
Wait, I'm coming with you!

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:00.040
Shit, I don't have the right grip!

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.400
Nemeth upgrade complete.

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:04.670
Power grid optimized.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:07.710
Delta 1, heading to open the connector covers.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:08.540
I'm going too!

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:11.510
All that's left is...

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:13.600
Second Lt. Hayate, respond!

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:14.830
First Lt. Mirage!

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:16.880
Connection is unstable.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:18.500
I'll try another route.

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:21.980
<i>Waiting... for you!</i>

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:23.360
<i>We're good... to go!</i>

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:37.610
This is bad.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:40.870
<i>Never be satisfied</i>

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:44.540
<i>Human desires are limitless</i>

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:45.440
Island ship block 18 breached.

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:47.250
<i>Inside and outside</i>

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:48.040
Emergency repair systems not functional.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:51.040
<i>There may be complicated emotions</i>

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:51.040
Captain, the island ship is going to run out of air!

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:57.230
<i>Pursue your desires all the way</i>

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:52.550
We've got no choice.

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:55.550
Macross Elysion, commence emergency docking!

00:17:57.230 --> 00:18:00.990
<i>Inside and outside</i>

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:59.800
This is Macross Elysion to all personnel!

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:05.130
We will commence emergency docking with the island jack pod ahead of schedule.

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:07.560
<i>Nothing is stable</i>

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.800
<i>Just... grab my...</i>

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.990
<i>It's hard to define</i>

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:08.520
Hayate?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.520
<i>Hold it... tight...</i>

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:13.970
<i>Feelings of loneliness, depression, and hopelessness</i>

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:13.020
<i>Okay!</i>

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:13.980
Mirage?

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:16.350
<i>Reality and dream</i>

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:18.030
<i>I'm telling you... to hold me... tight!</i>

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:20.130
<i>Get into a desperate situation</i>

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:22.060
<i>Is this... gonna work?</i>

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.460
What are they even doing?

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:26.550
<i>The different ages clash</i>

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:21.490
I don't wanna know.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.240
Put your focus on the stage!

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:26.740
Y-Yup!

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:30.050
<i>Reality and dream</i>

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:36.670
<i>It's all over now</i>

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:32.300
Just a little more!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.290
I told you to hold me!

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:38.300
<i>Neo nebula</i>

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:38.300
The Elysion?

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:43.070
<i>It's flashing, sparking, there's a burning flame</i>

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:43.260
It's the Macross!

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:49.210
<i>Small sparks of fire burn up into a flame</i>

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.770
Hold me down from closer!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.380
Hurry up!

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:52.270
<i>There's freedom in the galaxy</i>

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:51.920
Fine!

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:55.640
<i>uniting and coming into space</i>

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:56.790
Hold on tighter!

00:18:55.640 --> 00:19:02.490
<i>What appeared out of the blue was a whole new world</i>

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:58.280
R-Right on!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.500
You're up, Elysion!

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:18.670
Just a little more!

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:21.220
Did you learn nothing on Ragna?

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.760
Shut up! I know!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:29.730
I'll take back our sky!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:31.730
<i>Two mystic powers come together</i>

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.060
<i>Neo nebula</i>

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:37.780
<i>What a wonder; it's an amazing chemistry</i>

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:44.230
<i>They melt into one and light up the galaxy</i>

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:50.910
<i>Shining down onto a brand new world</i>

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:47.660
Island jack pod, power lines connected!

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:50.120
Emergency docking system is operational!

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:51.620
Okay!

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:54.130
<i>There's freedom in the galaxy</i>

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:54.130
Macross Elysion! Dock!

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.200
<i>uniting and coming into space</i>

00:19:57.200 --> 00:20:04.640
<i>What appeared out of the blue was a whole new world</i>

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:15.900
Good one!

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:21.250
The sky's back!

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:24.320
Walküre!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.210
Hell, yeah!

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:26.120
So cool!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.240
Thanks!

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:38.600
Wow!

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:40.400
It's like we're back on Ragna!

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:44.590
Good job, everyone.

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:46.810
We've just got a call.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:49.310
We found new sponsors.

00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:56.270
Lady M talked with some mining 
corporations in the globular cluster.

00:20:56.590 --> 00:21:00.730
We have a new mission: reclaim the cluster.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:02.150
Booyah!

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:05.580
Hey! Could someone please get us down from here?

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:08.160
Don't move! It's dangerous!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.910
Just focus on not letting go!

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:12.910
I really didn't want to know.

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:16.350
Haya-Haya! Mira-Mira! Good job!

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.790
Mission 14: Embracing Adrift

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:48.990
<i>I stand on the burning wreckage</i>

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:55.710
<i>I don't know for how long or why at all</i>

00:21:55.710 --> 00:22:00.470
<i>The flames around are drowning me</i>

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:06.970
<i>Finding what I seek feels so pointless now</i>

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:12.720
<i>Break the world and go beyond the ecstasy of the past</i>

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:19.100
<i>Choose the future even if it's the inferior option</i>

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:20.060
<i>Let's go</i>

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:23.070
<i>Love forever until the very end</i>

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:25.990
<i>Sing so hard until it hurts</i>

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:31.780
<i>Until your soul finally settles down</i>

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:34.690
<i>But if you still want to sing then</i>

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:37.520
<i>If you want to bet all on living</i>

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:43.340
<i>The purity of your heart will destroy everything</i>

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:48.290
<i>Everyone's a baby</i>

00:22:48.290 --> 00:22:55.020
<i>I'll forgive you in a chaotic climax</i>

00:22:56.550 --> 00:22:58.280
Valens charts, disconnected.

00:22:58.280 --> 00:22:59.530
Higgsbar, stable.

00:22:59.530 --> 00:23:00.920
Gravity, established.

00:23:00.920 --> 00:23:02.360
Sigur Valens, take off.

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:16.140
My father reclaimed our sky at the cost of his life.

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:22.180
I will inherit his will and guide the globular cluster.

00:23:22.180 --> 00:23:27.210
Are you truly ready to take over His Majesty's will?

00:23:27.940 --> 00:23:29.720
What do you mean?

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:32.090
I have...

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:34.600
...his will.

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:39.770
Next time: Parting Resolution
